flycast2021 (metallic77/flycast 603814c, ROCKNIX's flycast2021-lr pin):
the fork comments out PostProcessor::SelectFramebuffer's body, and the
comment swallows PostProcessor::Render's whole definition, so a GLES2 build
fails to link (gles.cpp still calls it when the PowerVR2 filter option is
on). An empty Render links it; with the filter on, nothing is
post-processed. The filter is off by default.

--- a/core/rend/gles/postprocess.cpp
+++ b/core/rend/gles/postprocess.cpp
@@ -353,3 +353,8 @@
    glClear(GL_COLOR_BUFFER_BIT);
    glDrawArrays(GL_TRIANGLE_STRIP, 0, 4);*/
 }
+
+// ZyperOS: this fork comments out SelectFramebuffer's body, and Render's whole
+// definition went inside that comment, so a GLES2 build failed to link. The
+// PowerVR2 filter that calls it is off; with it on, nothing is post-processed.
+void PostProcessor::Render(GLuint output_fbo) {}
